---
title: "Spacing"
description: "Padding and margin on the spacing scale."
section: Utilities
sectionOrder: 3
order: 3
---

A bare number is a step on the spacing scale (`--p: 4` is `4 × --spacing`). The named `--space-*` tokens map to 1, 2, 4, 6, 11, 24, and 40; use the number in `style`. Any length works too. Sides are `t`, `r`, `b`, `l` and set logical properties, so `l` is the right side in a right-to-left document. Margins also take `auto`.

